{
  "id": "imperativ",
  "name": "Imperative: Mange ! Sois, Aie, Va; Donne-le-moi",
  "level": "A2",
  "variety": "fr-FR",
  "subtitle": "The imperative gives an order, an instruction or a piece of advice, with no subject: Mange ! (tu), Mangeons ! (nous), Mangez ! (vous). With tu, -er verbs lose their -s. Pronouns follow the verb with a hyphen: Donne-le-moi. Prends-le.",
  "briefMarks": ["Mange", "Mangeons", "Mangez", "Sois", "Aie", "Va", "Ne parle pas", "Prends-le", "Lève-toi", "Ne le prends pas"],
  "source": "icanspeak French original text (grammar-a2 run, 2026-11-08)",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "(ne)", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "verb: tu / nous / vous", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "-le · -moi · -toi", "variant": "dat" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-verb\">Ouvrez</span> le dossier. · <span class=\"vp-verb\">Prenez</span> la deuxième rue. · <span class=\"vp-prep\">Ne</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">parle</span> <span class=\"vp-prep\">pas</span> fort ! · <span class=\"vp-verb\">Donne</span>-le-moi. · <span class=\"vp-prep\">Ne</span> <span class=\"vp-prep\">le</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">prends</span> <span class=\"vp-prep\">pas</span> !",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "The imperative has three forms and <strong>no subject</strong>: <strong>tu</strong> (a friend, a child), <strong>nous</strong> (let's) and <strong>vous</strong> (formal, or several people): <em>Parle ! Parlons ! Parlez !</em> At work, at the doctor's or in directions you mostly hear <em>vous</em>: <em>Ouvrez la bouche. Tournez à gauche.</em>",
        "tag": "tu, nous, vous"
      },
      {
        "html": "With <strong>tu</strong>, -er verbs lose the final <em>-s</em>: <em>Tu manges → Mange ! Tu parles → Parle !</em> Other verbs keep it: <em>Finis ! Prends ! Attends ! Fais !</em> Note: <em>Vas-y !</em> keeps the -s before <em>y</em>.",
        "tag": "-er verbs"
      },
      {
        "html": "Three irregular verbs: <strong>être</strong> → <em>sois, soyons, soyez</em>; <strong>avoir</strong> → <em>aie, ayons, ayez</em>; <strong>aller</strong> → <em>va, allons, allez</em>. <em>Sois à l'heure ! N'aie pas peur ! Allez tout droit.</em>",
        "tag": "être, avoir, aller"
      },
      {
        "html": "In the negative, <strong>ne … pas</strong> goes around the verb: <em>Ne parle pas fort ! Ne mangez pas ici. N'oublie pas ton badge.</em>",
        "tag": "Negative"
      },
      {
        "html": "In the <strong>affirmative</strong>, pronouns come <strong>after</strong> the verb, joined with hyphens. <em>me</em> and <em>te</em> become <em>moi</em> and <em>toi</em>: <em>Prends-le. Écoute-moi. Lève-toi. Donne-le-moi. Parle-lui.</em>",
        "tag": "Pronouns after"
      },
      {
        "html": "In the <strong>negative</strong>, pronouns go back <strong>before</strong> the verb and have their usual form: <em>Ne le prends pas. Ne me parle pas. Ne te lève pas.</em>",
        "tag": "Pronouns before"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Tu manges !</em> (as an order) → ✓ <em>Mange !</em> ✗ <em>Sois pas en retard</em> → ✓ <em>Ne sois pas en retard</em>. ✗ <em>Le prends</em> → ✓ <em>Prends-le</em>. ✗ <em>Ne prends-le pas</em> → ✓ <em>Ne le prends pas</em>. ✗ <em>Ne parle-moi pas</em> → ✓ <em>Ne me parle pas</em>. In fast speech <em>ne</em> disappears (<em>Fais pas ça !</em>); in writing and in polite speech keep it. Next: <a href=\"/object-pronouns\">le, la, les</a>, <a href=\"/indirect-object-pronouns\">lui, leur</a>, <a href=\"/reflexive-verbs\">reflexive verbs</a>.",
